tasks.brief:
The sign-in screen in public/index.html must work on a TV: no popup window, a 4-character code to type at plex.tv/link on a phone, and a same-tab sign-in for computers. Only public/index.html changes. It is a big file (about 3,000 lines): do NOT read it all. Search it for the quoted text below and read 40 lines around each place. The server side is done (T01): POST /auth/plex/start with JSON {mode:'link'} answers {code, linkUrl, qrUrl, expiresIn}; with {mode:'redirect'} answers {authUrl}; GET /auth/plex/poll answers {status:'pending'|'ok'|'expired'} or 403 {status:'denied', error} or 400 {status:'none', error}. The server keeps the pin in a cookie: the page never sends a pin id.

1. CSS. Find the line `#gate .status.error{color:var(--red);}` in the <style> block and add these lines right after it, exactly:

  #gate .gate-actions{display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:center; gap:12px;}
  #gate .btn-code{background:transparent; color:var(--text); border:1px solid var(--grid-line); border-radius:12px; padding:12px 22px; font-weight:600; font-size:13.5px; cursor:pointer;}
  #gate button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--cyan); outline-offset:3px;}
  #gate .link-panel{display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:center; gap:14px;}
  #gate .link-row{display:flex; align-items:center; gap:36px;}
  #gate .link-steps{display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:center; gap:6px;}
  /* While the code shows, the screen must fit a TV browser's 960x540 with nothing cut off. */
  #gate.coding{gap:12px;}
  #gate.coding .mark{width:60px; height:60px;}
  #gate.coding > p{display:none;}
  #gate .link-panel[hidden], #gate .gate-actions[hidden]{display:none;}
  #gate .link-panel p{font-size:16px; max-width:520px;}
  #gate .link-url{font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace; font-size:30px; font-weight:600; color:var(--cyan);}
  #gate .link-code{font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace; font-size:72px; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:.18em; padding-left:.18em; line-height:1.1; color:var(--text);}
  #gate .link-qr{width:132px; height:132px; background:#fff; border-radius:10px; padding:6px;}
  #gate .link-qr[hidden]{display:none;}

2. HTML. Inside <div id="gate">, replace the whole `<button class="btn-plex" onclick="startSignIn()"> ... </button>` (4 lines) with this, exactly, and leave the `<div class="status" id="gate-status"></div>` line that follows it in place:

  <div class="gate-actions" id="gate-actions">
    <button class="btn-plex" id="btn-signin" onclick="startSignIn()">
      <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M4 2h9.62L22 12l-8.38 10H4l8.38-10z"/></svg>
      Sign in with Plex
    </button>
    <button class="btn-code" id="btn-code" onclick="startCodeSignIn()">On a TV? Sign in with a code</button>
  </div>
  <div class="link-panel" id="link-panel" hidden>
    <div class="link-row">
      <div class="link-steps">
        <p>On your phone or computer, go to</p>
        <div class="link-url" id="link-url">plex.tv/link</div>
        <p>sign in to Plex, and enter this code</p>
        <div class="link-code" id="link-code"></div>
      </div>
      <img class="link-qr" id="link-qr" alt="QR code for plex.tv/link" hidden>
    </div>
    <button class="btn-code" id="btn-back" onclick="cancelSignIn()">Back</button>
  </div>

3. JavaScript. Find `async function startSignIn(){` and replace that whole function (it ends just before `async function signOut(){`) with the functions below. window.open must not appear anywhere in the file afterwards.
   - `let signInTimer = null; let codeRenewals = 0;`
   - isTvBrowser(): true when `new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('tv') === '1'`, or when navigator.userAgent matches /\bTV\b|SMART-TV|SmartTV|Tizen|Web0S|WebOS|BRAVIA|AFT[A-Z]|CrKey|Roku|VIDAA|HbbTV|LacklusterPlusTV/i.
   - gateStatus(text, isError): sets #gate-status textContent to text (or '') and toggles its class 'error' with `classList.toggle('error', !!isError)`.
   - showCodePanel(on): `#link-panel`.hidden = !on; `#gate-actions`.hidden = on; `#gate`.classList.toggle('coding', on).
   - showGateChoices(): clearInterval(signInTimer); showCodePanel(false); then focus #btn-code when isTvBrowser() else #btn-signin (`.focus()`).
   - cancelSignIn(): showGateChoices(); gateStatus('').
   - pollSignIn(): clearInterval(signInTimer); signInTimer = setInterval(async () => {...}, 2000). Each tick: fetch('/auth/plex/poll') and read its JSON inside try/catch (on a network error just return and try again next tick). If body.status === 'pending' return. Otherwise clearInterval(signInTimer) and: 'ok' -> gateStatus('Signed in!'); showCodePanel(false); checkAuth(). 'expired' -> if the code panel is showing (`!document.getElementById('link-panel').hidden`) and codeRenewals < 8: codeRenewals++ and startCodeSignIn(true) (a fresh code replaces the old one by itself); else showGateChoices() and gateStatus('That sign-in ran out of time - try again.', true). Anything else (denied, none) -> showGateChoices(); gateStatus(body.error || 'Sign-in did not work - try again.', true).
   - async startCodeSignIn(isRenewal): if (isRenewal !== true) codeRenewals = 0. (The button calls it with a click event, so compare with true.) gateStatus('Getting a code...'). In try/catch: POST /auth/plex/start with headers {'Content-Type':'application/json'} and body JSON.stringify({mode:'link'}); if !res.ok throw. Put info.code into #link-code (textContent). Put info.linkUrl without its https:// into #link-url. For the QR: `const qr = document.getElementById('link-qr'); qr.hidden = true;` and if info.qrUrl: qr.onload = () => { qr.hidden = false; }; qr.onerror = () => { qr.hidden = true; }; qr.src = info.qrUrl. Then showCodePanel(true); focus #btn-back; gateStatus('Waiting for you to enter the code...'); pollSignIn(). In the catch: showGateChoices(); gateStatus('Something went wrong getting a code - try again.', true).
   - async startSignIn(): gateStatus('Opening Plex sign-in...'). In try/catch: POST /auth/plex/start with the JSON body {mode:'redirect'}; if !res.ok throw; then `location.assign(info.authUrl)` - THIS tab goes to Plex, no new window. In the catch: gateStatus('Something went wrong starting sign-in.', true).
   - startGate(): `const params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);` If params.get('signin') === 'return' (the browser is back from Plex): params.delete('signin'); `const q = params.toString(); history.replaceState(null, '', location.pathname + (q ? '?' + q : ''));` hide #gate-actions; gateStatus('Finishing sign-in...'); pollSignIn(). Else if isTvBrowser(): startCodeSignIn(). Else: showGateChoices().

4. In checkAuth(), in the `else` branch (nobody is signed in), after the two lines that show #gate and hide #app, add `startGate();`.

Change nothing else in the file. Run the test: .venv\Scripts\python.exe tests\test_signin_page.py - it starts the gateway and a headless browser itself (about a minute). tests\test_signin_api.py must still pass.
